senses.gloss:
√1su (sunóti, sunuté; suṣā́va; saviṣyáti,
soṣyáti; sutá; -sútya). press out, extráct,
 esp. the Soma or éxtract; sunvánt,
as m. the Soma-presser; --sutá, extracted;
as m. the éxtract, i. e. Soma-juice, 70^5;
draught of Soma, 73^10.

√sū or su (sū́te [628]; suṣā́va, suṣuvé;
ásoṣṭa; saviṣyáti, -te; soṣyáti, -te;
sūtá, sutá; sūtvā́; -sū́ya). generate;
bring forth; bear; so perhaps at RV. x.
125. 7. [cf. 2suta, ‘bairn’; υἱὀς, *συ-ιο-ς,
‘son’; for pronunciation as trisyllable,
ὑ-ι-ός, cf. Boeotian οὑιός: see also under
sū́ and sūnú.]
+ pra, bring forth; prasūta, born of
(gen.).
